    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# ENCH 680 Course Project: Reproducing Yuan et al. (2021)\n",
        "**Applied Machine Learning for Prediction of CO₂ Adsorption on Biomass Waste-Derived Porous Carbons**\n",
        "*Environ. Sci. Technol.* 2021, 55, 11925–11936. https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.1c01849\n",
        "\n",
        "Group members: Kyra Kjargaard, Henry Pedraza Martinez. University of Calgary, ENCH 680.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What this notebook does**\n",
        "1. Loads the authors' dataset (527 data points), [authors' GitHub repository](https://github.com/ssuvarnamanu/CO2-adsorption-by-biowaste-based-porous-carbon).\n",
        "2. Repeats the preprocessing: random-forest imputation of TPV and MPV from SA, then drops S (%).\n",
        "3. Trains the Chapter 3 baselines (a single decision tree with and without pre-pruning, and a random forest).\n",
        "4. Approximate reproduction with modern libraries, not identical methodology of the the paper's three boosted-tree models (GBDT, XGBoost, LightGBM) with an 85/15 split, 5-fold CV and grid search.\n",
        "5. Compares our results with Table 1 of the paper.\n",
        "6. Interprets the model with permutation importance (MDA).\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OAvOCBm9hI2Y"
      }
    },
    {
