        "##7. Model interpretation: permutation importance (MDA) and partial dependence\n",
        "The paper uses permutation importance (mean decrease in accuracy). Chapter 3 warns that impurity-based importance can be misleading when features are correlated (SA, TPV, MPV), so permutation importance on the test set is the safer choice."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AHIvzaBhCtd3"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "gbdt = models[best]\n",
        "pi = permutation_importance(gbdt, X_test, y_test, n_repeats=30, random_state=SEED, scoring=\"r2\")\n",
        "imp_df = pd.DataFrame({\"feature\": FEATURES, \"MDA (drop in R²)\": pi.importances_mean, \"std\": pi.importances_std,\n",
        "                       \"impurity importance\": gbdt.feature_importances_}).sort_values(\"MDA (drop in R²)\", ascending=True)\n",
        "RESULTS[\"importance\"] = imp_df.round(4).to_dict(orient=\"records\")\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4.8))\n",
        "ax.barh(imp_df[\"feature\"], imp_df[\"MDA (drop in R²)\"], xerr=imp_df[\"std\"], color=\"#1F4E79\")\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Mean decrease in test R² when feature is shuffled\"); ax.set_title(\"GBDT permutation feature importance\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(\"figs/fig4_permutation_importance.png\", dpi=200); plt.show()\n",
        "imp_df.sort_values(\"MDA (drop in R²)\", ascending=False).round(3)"
      ],
